{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinSurrealGrade","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinSurrealGrade","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","lean:module:QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade","lean:module:QOU.Information.CountingModuliGrade","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Ordinal.Arithmetic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_id_of_birthday_horizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_id_of_birthday_horizon","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L166-L177","doc":"**Surreal-grade reading of the per-state horizon separation (sorry-free).**\nIf the observed output of `P` is reached no earlier than its birthday-shadow\nhorizon cost `3^{len P}`, then `P` is not poly-observable under the identity\nbudget — the single-instance shadow of the level gap. Re-exposes the corpus\nbridge lemma `not_polyObservable_id_of_horizon_cost` in surreal-grade\nlanguage. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physicalCost_levelGeOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physicalCost_levelGeOne","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L157-L162","doc":"**Re-derivation cross-check (sorry-free).**  Applying the main brick to the\nboundary family recovers `physicalCost_superPoly`: the corpus's proved\n`#P`-hard boundary cost is exactly the level-≥1 verdict of this brick. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen_boundary_eq_physicalCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen_boundary_eq_physicalCost","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L147-L155","doc":"**The boundary family recovers the corpus physical cost (sorry-free).**  The\n`NP`-boundary family has `c = 3N` crossings and `len =` crossing count, so\n`lenFamily n = 3n` and `horizonCostOfLen (3·) = physicalCost = 3^{3n}`.\nAnchors the abstract length grade to the already-proved `#P`-over-moduli\nresult. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_levelZero_horizonCostOfLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_levelZero_horizonCostOfLen","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**No polynomial budget bounds the length-graded horizon cost (sorry-free).**\nThe main brick composed with the level gap: under at-least-linear length\ngrowth, no `c·nᵏ` dominates `3^{len}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen_levelGeOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen_levelGeOne","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**MAIN BRICK (sorry-free) — the length filtration's ω-grade is level ≥ 1.**\nConditional on at-least-linear length growth `hlin`, the horizon cost\n`3^{len}` occupies transseries level ≥ 1: `ord_ω(3^{len}) > ord_ω(budget)`.\nThe hypothesis `hlin` is the honest input (length really grows with size);\nthe grade is derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.two_pow_le_horizonCostOfLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.two_pow_le_horizonCostOfLen","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**`2ⁿ ≤ 3^{lenFamily n}` under at-least-linear length growth (sorry-free).**\nIf the filtration level grows at least linearly in problem size\n(`n ≤ lenFamily n`), the horizon cost dominates `2ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonCostOfLen","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L112-L115","doc":"**The horizon cost as a function of a length family**: `3` to the\nfiltration level `lenFamily n` (the surviving `3^{len}` skein resolution\ntree at problem size `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_levelZero_of_exp_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_levelZero_of_exp_growth","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**Exponential growth ⇒ no polynomial budget (sorry-free).**  Composition of\nthe conditional with the level gap: an exponentially-growing cost is not\npolynomially bounded — the surreal `ord_ω(cost) > ord_ω(budget)` conclusion,\nwith the growth bound as the sole hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.levelGeOne_of_exp_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.levelGeOne_of_exp_growth","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**Exponential growth forces level ≥ 1 (sorry-free) — THE conditional.**\nThe *hypothesis is the exponential growth bound* `2ⁿ ≤ g n`; the level-≥1\ngrade is *derived* (formalize-first: the growth bound is the honest input).\nRoutes through `superPoly_two_pow` (Mathlib little-o) lifted along `≤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.level_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.level_gap","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**The level gap (sorry-free)** — the two transseries bands are disjoint: a\nlevel-≥1 function is not level-0. This is the ω-grade squeeze\n`ord_ω(cost) > ord_ω(budget)`, the honest machine-checked core of the\n`P ⊊ EXP` band separation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.LevelGeOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.LevelGeOne","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L83-L85","doc":"**Level ≥ 1** — the exponential-or-higher band: `ord_ω(g) > ord_ω(nᵏ)` for\nevery `k`. Exp is transseries level 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.LevelZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.LevelZero","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L79-L81","doc":"**Level 0** — the polynomial (archimedean) band: `ord_ω(g) ≤ ord_ω(nᵏ)`.\nPoly is transseries level 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.birthdayShadow_lt_omega0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.birthdayShadow_lt_omega0","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L67-L75","doc":"**A single state sits in the finite (archimedean) birthday band\n(sorry-free).**  Its birthday shadow is `< ω`: the exponential blow-up is\nin the *cost as a function of* the length, never in the length of one\nword. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.birthdayShadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.birthdayShadow","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinSurrealGrade.lean#L58-L65","doc":"**Birthday shadow** of a state: the finite ordinal equal to its `ℕ`-valued\nlength filtration. A finite braid word's surreal sign-expansion length is\nliterally its `ℕ` length, and the birthday of a finite ordinal `n` is `n`,\nso `len` is the finite (archimedean, birthday `< ω`) shadow of the surreal\nlength. ","signatureChunk":0}]}